                <mxCell id="o_e5" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;dashed=1;" parent="1" source="o_aL" target="o_aF1" edge="1">
                    <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="o_e6" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;dashed=1;" parent="1" source="o_bL" target="o_bF1" edge="1">
                    <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="o_tradeoffs" value="KEY TRADE-OFFS&#xa;&#xa;- Raft/quorum store (etcd, ZooKeeper) vs Redis: majority-commit before ack → mutual exclusion survives failover. Redis async replication can lose an acked lock → double-grant. Cost: higher write latency.&#xa;- CP vs AP: refuse on minority partition to never double-grant. Cost: minority unavailable.&#xa;- Many Raft groups (sharded keyspace) vs one group: scales writes past one leader&#39;s ~10-30k/s. Cost: rebalancing, hot-shard risk, no cheap cross-key txn.&#xa;- Watch/notify vs spin-retry: idle waiters → ~1 write per ownership change. Cost: push/session mgmt, missed-notification handling.&#xa;- Fencing token enforced AT the resource vs trust the lock: only resource-side monotonic check stops a paused holder writing." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=#b85450;fillColor=#f8cecc;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="60" y="1280" width="700" height="280" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="o_deep" value="DEEP DIVES&#xa;&#xa;- Core hard problem: single agreed holder under node failure → consensus (Raft), ack only after majority log-commit.&#xa;- Scale-break: 1M writes/s ≪ one Raft leader (~10-30k/s) → 50-100 range-partitioned Raft groups (etcd/TiKV range model).&#xa;- Hot lock (e.g. leader:cluster-A, 200k acquire/s on ONE key): can&#39;t shard a single key, can&#39;t replicate a writable lock. Fix = watches + client backoff + lease-based election; isolate hot key in its own group/hardware; batch log appends.&#xa;- Consistency: linearizable acquire via quorum; reads via leader-lease or quorum read.&#xa;- Fencing: monotonic token in the Raft log; downstream resource rejects stale tokens.&#xa;- Operability: per-key write-rate metrics + alerts to detect hot shards; fleet cost of N 5-node groups; blast radius = one key-range unavailable when its leader is down (OK under CP); watch/session expiry + missed-notification reconciliation." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fillColor=#dae8fc;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="1080" y="1290" width="720" height="280" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
            </root>
        </mxGraphModel>
    </diagram>
</mxfile>